-- check/bad: an operator section passed as an argument
-- (`docs/design/static-dispatch-spike.md` §3.1, Appendix A.22). Its type is
-- known exactly — `number, number -> Bool` — so the mistake is reported
-- where it is made, against `foldl`'s 3rd parameter, and not inside the
-- lambda the section desugars to: type_mismatch at 10:25 naming `foldl`.
-- With the section's type left to the body, this read "This is `Bool` but I
-- need `b`" and pointed at the same place for a different reason.
pub folded : Int
folded = List.foldl [ 1 ] 0 (<)
